Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"

SIT Internal

Greetings Students of Group 11,

Please find the following information for your assigned AWS EC2:
Access IP: 13.59.88.187
Username: student11
Key (attached): ICT2212-AY26-T1-student11.pem

If you are using putty to access the EC2, please first convert the key to .ppk format before using it with putty.
You may find the instructions and download link here:

  1.  Convert Pem to Ppk File Using PuTTYgen<https://www.puttygen.com/convert-pem-to-ppk#Converting_Pem_to_Ppk_on_Windows>
  2.  Download Putty for Windows, Linux and Mac - Install SSH in PuTTY (puttygen.com)<https://www.puttygen.com/download-putty>

Or you may use the following windows command (for latest WinOS) to access the EC2:
ssh -i "C:\<Directory-to-key>\ICT2212-AY26-T1-student11.pem" student11@13.59.88.187
Note: Ensure the pem file access permission is allowable by your own windows account only.

If there is any issue with the EC2, you may contact us at the following email or through MSTeams with up to 1-2 Working Days:

  1.  William - William.tan@singaporetech.edu.sg<mailto:William.tan@singaporetech.edu.sg>
  2.  Myat - Myat.HtikeKo@Singaporetech.edu.sg<mailto:Myat.HtikeKo@Singaporetech.edu.sg>

TO READ AND NOTE:
1. Always remember to back up your files and config. The EC2 will be reset if there is no way of recovering and all the files will be lost.
2. Always test any major config changes or firewall changes on a locally hosted VM first.
3. Always remember to add TCP 22 (or any other port) for your SSH connection when configuring your EC2 firewall rules (ufw.rules).
4. Always remember to include your Module name and AWS EC2 Username when contacting us.
5. ONLY circulate or share your access IP, username and key file within your group members unless instructed otherwise.


--_000_TYZPR01MB7075B71D47CDB84F89497EB1D4B62TYZPR01MB7075apcp_
