<body lang="EN-SG" link="#0563C1" vlink="#96607D" style="word-wrap:break-word">
<p style="font-family:Calibri;font-size:12pt;color:#000000;margin:5pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;" align="Center">
SIT Internal<br>
</p>
<br>
<div>
<div class="WordSection1">
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">Greetings </span><span lang="EN-US">Students</span><span lang="EN-US"> of Group
</span><span lang="EN-US">11</span><span lang="EN-US">,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">Please find the following information for your assigned AWS EC2:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">Access IP: </span><b><u><span lang="EN-US">13.59.88.187</span></u></b><b><u><span lang="EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">Username: </span><b><u><span lang="EN-US">student11</span></u></b><b><u><span lang="EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">Key (attached): </span><b><u><span lang="EN-US">ICT2212-AY26-T1-student11.pem</span></u></b><b><u><span lang="EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><b><u><span lang="EN-US"><o:p><span style="text-decoration:none">&nbsp;</span></o:p></span></u></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">If you are using putty to access the EC2, please first convert the key to .ppk format before using it with putty.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">You may find the instructions and download link here:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<ol style="margin-top:0cm" start="1" type="1">
<li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0cm;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2"><a href="https://www.puttygen.com/convert-pem-to-ppk#Converting_Pem_to_Ppk_on_Windows">Convert Pem to Ppk File Using PuTTYgen</a><o:p></o:p></li><li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0cm;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2"><a href="https://www.puttygen.com/download-putty">Download Putty for Windows, Linux and Mac - Install SSH in PuTTY (puttygen.com)</a><span lang="EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">Or you may use the following windows command (for latest WinOS) to access the EC2:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="background:#F2F2F2"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black">ssh -i &#8220;C:\&lt;Directory-to-key&gt;\</span></b><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black">ICT2212-AY26-T1-student11.pem</span></b><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black">&#8221;
</span></b><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black">student11</span></b><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black">@</span></b><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black">13.59.88.187</span></b><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">Note: Ensure the pem file access permission is allowable by your own windows account only.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">If there is any issue with the EC2, you may contact us at the following email or through MSTeams with up to
<u>1-2</u> Working Days:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<ol style="margin-top:0cm" start="1" type="1">
<li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0cm;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo4"><span lang="EN-US">William &#8211;
</span><a href="mailto:William.tan@singaporetech.edu.sg"><span lang="EN-US">William.tan@singaporetech.edu.sg</span></a><span lang="EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0cm;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo4"><span lang="EN-US">Myat &#8211;
</span><a href="mailto:Myat.HtikeKo@Singaporetech.edu.sg"><span lang="EN-US">Myat.HtikeKo@Singaporetech.edu.sg</span></a><o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><u><span lang="EN-US" style="color:red">TO READ AND NOTE:
<o:p></o:p></span></u></i></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><span lang="EN-US" style="color:red">1. Always remember to back up your files and config. The EC2 will be reset if there is no way of recovering and all the files will be lost.<o:p></o:p></span></i></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><span lang="EN-US" style="color:red">2. Always test any major config changes or firewall changes on
<u>a locally hosted VM</u> first.<o:p></o:p></span></i></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><span lang="EN-US" style="color:red">3. Always remember to add TCP 22 (or any other port) for your SSH connection when configuring your EC2 firewall rules (ufw.rules).<o:p></o:p></span></i></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><span lang="EN-US" style="color:red">4. Always remember to include your Module name and AWS EC2 Username when contacting us.<o:p></o:p></span></i></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><span lang="EN-US" style="color:red">5. <u>ONLY</u> circulate or share your access IP, username and key file within your group members unless instructed otherwise.<o:p></o:p></span></i></b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
</div>
